Renewable energy in manufacturing dramatically reduces carbon intensity and eliminates dependence on finite fossil fuel supplies, directly supporting circular economy objectives of resource regeneration. Products manufactured with renewable energy have substantially lower embodied carbon regardless of material choice, making this a high-leverage design decision. Additionally, designing for renewable energy production on-site or through clean grids can become a point of product differentiation and consumer value. From a circular perspective, renewable energy aligns with the principle that economic systems should operate within planetary boundaries.